# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository and on checkout,
# regardless of a contributor's local core.autocrlf setting. This avoids
# platform-dependent diff noise and, more importantly, avoids silently
# rewriting bytes in files whose checksums are recorded elsewhere in this
# repository (see the exceptions below and engine-src/README.md point 4
# for a real instance of this going wrong during Phase 0 development).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Upstream-verified files: their exact bytes are hashed and recorded in
# src-tauri/resources/pgn-extract/SOURCE.json, THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, and
# engine-src/upstream.lock. Disable line-ending conversion entirely so a
# checkout can never drift from the recorded checksum.
LICENSE -text
src-tauri/resources/pgn-extract/COPYING -text
src-tauri/resources/pgn-extract/eco.pgn -text

# Test fixtures: several files under fixtures/ deliberately test exact
# byte content (CRLF vs LF line endings, a UTF-8 BOM). Never let git
# normalize line endings here in either direction - see fixtures/README.md.
fixtures/** -text

# Binary assets.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
